00:05:00,000 --> 00:05:06,000
This Cop Plays Dirty!

2
00:10:00,000 --> 00:10:06,000
The Stone Killer is a crime, action film directed by Michael Winner.

3
00:15:00,000 --> 00:15:06,000
A Los Angeles detective is sent to New York where he must solve a
case involving an old Sicilian Mafia family feud.

4
00:20:00,000 --> 00:20:06,000
Lou Torrey, played by Charles Bronson.

5
00:25:00,000 --> 00:25:06,000
Al Vescari, played by Martin Balsam.

6
00:30:00,000 --> 00:30:06,000
Jumper, played by Jack Colvin.

7
00:35:00,000 --> 00:35:06,000
Langley, played by Paul Koslo.

8
00:40:00,000 --> 00:40:06,000
Les Daniels, played by Norman Fell.

9
00:45:00,000 --> 00:45:06,000
Guido Lorenz, played by David Sheiner.

10
00:50:00,000 --> 00:50:06,000
The Stone Killer is a 1973 American action neo noir thriller film produced
and directed by Michael Winner and starring Charles Bronson.

11
00:55:00,000 --> 00:55:06,000
It came out in between The Mechanic (1972) and Death Wish (1974), all
three of which teamed up actor/director Bronson and Winner.

12
01:00:00,000 --> 01:00:06,000
Norman Fell and John Ritter appear as cops in this film, not too long
before they would reunite for the TV series Three's Company.

13
01:05:00,000 --> 01:05:06,000
Ritter would also soon be reunited with co-star Ralph Waite for The Waltons.

14
01:10:00,000 --> 01:10:06,000
Character actor Stuart Margolin plays a significant
role; he also appeared in Death Wish.

15
01:15:00,000 --> 01:15:06,000
It was one of many Dirty Harry-type films featuring rogue cops who don't "play by
the rules" that were released in the wake of that film's success.

16
01:20:00,000 --> 01:20:06,000
Cristina Raines can briefly be seen as the daughter of Waite's character; Winner
would later hire Raines for the leading role in The Sentinel.

17
01:25:00,000 --> 01:25:06,000
The film explores themes of new york city, showdown, based
on novel or book, war veteran, gangster.

18
01:30:00,000 --> 01:30:06,000
The tone is dark.
